WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- We only have a little time left,

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.200
but first I am so happy to announce

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.121
our first show baby.

00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:09.113
(audience claps)

00:00:09.113 --> 00:00:12.160
(screams) Congrats to our writer Christina

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.360
and her husband, Danny

00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:16.803
on the birth of Martha Millie Namchack.

00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:18.989
(audience applauds)

00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:20.750
Martha Millie Namchack
welcome to the world.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.952
Buckle up it's gonna be a bumpy ride.

00:00:22.952 --> 00:00:26.130
But I promise you're gonna love it.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.930
And we're gonna love you right back.

00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:31.788
So hi BFFs!

00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:32.703
How ya doing?

00:00:32.703 --> 00:00:35.500
Wait we have a little
surprise in our audience.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.910
Phil, how ya doing?

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.603
Were you at last night's Emmy's?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.950
- Hi Drew, yes I was.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.443
- Oh yes! We've got an Emmy hazmat man.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.790
Thank you Phil for
coming here. How was it?

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.550
How was it?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.063
- It was incredible.
It was such a fun show.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.835
I was stationed at Hugh
Jackman so that was crazy.

00:00:54.835 --> 00:00:58.210
- I just have to say, your outfit,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.890
you are giving it. This
is a tux 2020 style.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.813
I am so in. Thank you for coming.

00:01:04.813 --> 00:01:05.646
- Thank you

00:01:05.646 --> 00:01:07.800
- We loved you guys last night.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.550
Okay Erin I heard there was
another question from Erin.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.864
Hello Erin?

00:01:13.864 --> 00:01:17.300
- Hi yes. I read your autobiography

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.860
when I was in high school and
I have a question for you.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.570
Which I absolutely loved it.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.460
How have your life experiences

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.450
shaped the mother you are today?

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.090
- Oh my god entirely.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.110
First of all my parents
kind of gave me a blueprint

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.260
of everything not to do. Checkity check.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.580
Then I really took all
my life experiences,

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.950
and instead of speaking
negatively about them

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.850
to my children, cause
I don't feel that way.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.710
I love and embrace all of them,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.870
but it has turned me into
a mother who really cares

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.470
about the pillars of appropriateness,

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:50.593
and how to be safe and stay
young as long as possible.

00:01:52.293 --> 00:01:54.990
So really all of our life
lessons should be lessons to us

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.440
and our kids. Not our
weaknesses, but our strengths.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.550
Thank you for asking that question, Erin.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:04.583
And to everyone at home. Thank
you so much for joining us.

